sam: Heads-up — ran into a reproducible TS typing loss when our JS SDK is consumed from a bundled ESM edge app. Generics/overloads collapse to any.

lina: ouch. minimal repro?

sam: gist of the SDK API: 
```ts
// sdk/src/api.ts
export function fetchTyped<T>(input: T): Promise<{ out: T }>;
export function fetchTyped(input: unknown) { return Promise.resolve({ out: input as any }); }
```
consumer:
```ts
import { fetchTyped } from '@redwood/sdk';
type Q = { name: string };
async function main(){
  const r = await fetchTyped<Q>({ name: 'x' });
  // expected r.out: Q — in Edge ESM build r.out is any (no completions)
}
```

kevin: does CJS keep the typings?

sam: yes. dist/cjs/index.d.ts has overloads. dist/esm/index.d.ts in the package tarball shows a single widened signature. We use esbuild to produce the ESM entry which is a small re-export wrapper: `export * from './lib'` — seems like declaration merging got lost.

maria: check package.json "types" and exports map. TS will pick different .d.ts depending on exports/types and module resolution. Also check if bundler rewrote the .d.ts during publish.

sam: types -> "dist/types/index.d.ts" but the published esm entry also shipped its own index.d.ts (generated by the bundler) which appears to have collapsed signatures.

kevin: short fixes: 1) point the ESM export to the compiled file that has preserved d.ts, 2) generate a single hand-curated index.d.ts for the public API that lists overloads, or 3) change build to emit declarations from source rather than from bundle.

lina: and add a small CI check that emits declarations for both cjs and esm artifacts and fails if public API differs.

types-bot: Created ticket RW-DX-6312: "ESM bundle causes SDK generic overloads to widen to any for Edge consumers" (triaged).

maria: docs note: mention workaround (deep import to cjs entry or pin version) and a snippet to detect the issue: `npx tsc --showConfig && npx tsc -p . --declaration --emitDeclarationOnly` run against node_modules entry.

kevin: i'll pick this up. plan: add declaration-emit CI, switch esm package entry to avoid wrapper, and if needed add explicit d.ts. I'll post PR.

sam: thanks — will attach repro and a tiny vercel edge test to the ticket to catch regressions. :thumbsup:
